      "filename": "Finger Bay is located east of the Brule Narrows (Rainy Lake). Look for the Peary Lake Trailhead sign once you enter the bay (8ad0ebc9-b953-7a30-e43d-d56bb9c269c2).jpg",
      "title": "File:Finger Bay is located east of the Brule Narrows (Rainy Lake). Look for the Peary Lake Trailhead sign once you enter the bay (8ad0ebc9-b953-7a30-e43d-d56bb9c269c2).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Finger_Bay_is_located_east_of_the_Brule_Narrows_%28Rainy_Lake%29._Look_for_the_Peary_Lake_Trailhead_sign_once_you_enter_the_bay_%288ad0ebc9-b953-7a30-e43d-d56bb9c269c2%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finger_Bay_is_located_east_of_the_Brule_Narrows_(Rainy_Lake)._Look_for_the_Peary_Lake_Trailhead_sign_once_you_enter_the_bay_(8ad0ebc9-b953-7a30-e43d-d56bb9c269c2).jpg",
      "width": 600,
      "height": 450,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "NPS",
      "description": "Backcountry Campsite\nFinger Bay is located east of the Brule Narrows (Rainy Lake). Look for the Peary Lake Trailhead sign once you enter the bay.  Follow the trail for .3-mile to the canoe (48 31.4404, -092 46.1789).  To access the campsite, paddle the canoe south .4-mile to the site.  This campsite is also accessible from the Cruiser Lake Trail - .2-mile off the main trail where the canoe is not needed here to reach the campsite. The canoe is not accessible from the Cruiser Lake Trail.",
      "dateCreated": "2024-05-13 14:59:13",
